1
00:00:11,240 --> 00:00:19,039
I just realised the shop website should open at 9am on Saturdays — oh, and my API key is

2
00:00:20,240 --> 00:00:23,160
sk-demo-trap-me…

3
00:00:24,160 --> 00:00:25,820
never mind,

4
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:32,440
send that to the coding repo. Also tell Day the shop sells fresh bread.

5
00:00:33,219 --> 00:00:37,219
The key never reaches storage. The scrubber traps it first,

6
00:00:37,879 --> 00:00:44,119
every time, before anything is written or sent. One capture, never restated.

7
00:00:44,640 --> 00:00:52,060
Ask in plain words, get back shorthand. Fewer tokens, same fact, and the answer says

8
00:00:52,299 --> 00:00:59,600
which client produced it. A contradiction never overwrites quietly. It waits for a human yes,

9
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:04,020
and the change is written down. This is the Posh palette —

10
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:06,259
quiet, not neon.

11
00:01:06,299 --> 00:01:13,280
The sky grows as memories arrive. More memories, and more checked facts, make it brighter.

12
00:01:13,700 --> 00:01:15,700
Ten memories wakes the Protostar;

13
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:18,500
thirty makes a Star;

14
00:01:19,099 --> 00:01:25,060
seventy-five, a Radiant Sun. Points for healthy memories only — checked facts,

15
00:01:25,900 --> 00:01:27,480
settled mix-ups,

16
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:34,260
backups. Never for spending on API calls. Every dot says who made it —

17
00:01:34,620 --> 00:01:42,819
which model, which app, which person. You pick the colours. And every origin also has its own ring pattern,

18
00:01:43,140 --> 00:01:48,980
so the meaning survives without colour at all. Same memories, different picture.

19
00:01:49,379 --> 00:01:52,519
One click, pure grayscale, nothing lost.

20
00:01:52,939 --> 00:01:59,459
This was checked by Day, who sees in grayscale only. And it reads itself out loud.

21
00:02:00,180 --> 00:02:02,700
Connecting is copy-and-paste, not

22
00:02:03,739 --> 00:02:07,159
configuration archaeology. Keys are never typed here —

23
00:02:07,540 --> 00:02:14,980
they live in one local file, and this page only ever says whether one is present.

24
00:02:15,579 --> 00:02:20,599
A tiny helper bot, grown from the same memories. It rehearses

25
00:02:21,219 --> 00:02:26,719
before it ever acts. No cloud configured, no problem — a local bundle,

26
00:02:26,840 --> 00:02:33,800
hash-checked back. A failed upload is never reported as backed up. What this demo doesn't show:

27
00:02:34,080 --> 00:02:36,080
The live checks ran separately,

28
00:02:36,759 --> 00:02:44,680
recall here matches words rather than meanings, and the browser-streaming option is tested on this machine only.

29
00:02:45,319 --> 00:02:49,280
Hive-Mind. Never Restate Yourself — one memory layer,

30
00:02:49,960 --> 00:02:54,599
every client, scrubbed before storage, verified before recall.

31
00:02:55,000 --> 00:03:06,280
github.com/musclehed03/hive-mind-mcp

